SUDO - run a command as root
Usage: sudo <command> [args]
       echo <password> | sudo -S <command> [args]

Runs a command with administrator privileges. You must be in the
sudo group (the first user account is added automatically).

Authentication is cached for five minutes. In a window terminal,
pipe the password with -S.

Examples:
  sudo apt install fortune
  sudo useradd bob
  echo secret | sudo -S whoami

Notes:
- sudo whoami prints root.
- File writes under /etc require root.
